('gatlinburg-pigeon-forge','Gatlinburg / Pigeon Forge','Pigeon Forge, TN','TN',35.79,-83.55,
 'The most reliable lodging market in the country for exactly what we need: dozens of 8- to 12-bedroom cabins with private indoor pools, arcade rooms and theaters, every bedroom a real room. Great Smoky Mountains National Park is minutes away and Dollywood works for a 4-year-old and an 11-year-old. The cost is the travel day: no nonstop from Seattle to Knoxville, so the Washington family flies to Nashville and drives 3.5 hours. June brings high-80s humidity, afternoon storms and Parkway traffic.',
 '["Deepest 7+ bedroom inventory anywhere; the house will not be a fight","Best kid range on the list: Dollywood, aquarium, Anakeesta, caverns, tubing","Smokies adjacent: Cades Cove, Laurel Falls, elk at Cataloochee","Cabins are cheap for what you get"]',
 '["Worst travel day on the list for Seattle (about 10.5 hours, 3.5 of them in a car seat)","Southwest Florida has no clean nonstop either","June heat, humidity, storms and Parkway traffic"]',
 '{"lodging":{"score":25,"why":"Dozens of 8-12 BR cabins across half a dozen managers; nine months out still fine."},"amenities":{"score":10,"why":"Private indoor pools, game rooms and theaters are standard at this size."},"travel":{"score":12,"why":"Seattle: SEA-BNA nonstop plus a 3.5 h drive, ~10.5 h door to door. Nashville drives; Illinois/Wisconsin fly ORD/MKE-TYS; SW Florida connects or drives."},"kids":{"score":15,"why":"Dollywood, Ripley''s Aquarium, Anakeesta, WonderWorks, Tuckaleechee Caverns, Little River tubing; rainy-day options everywhere."},"nature":{"score":14,"why":"Great Smoky Mountains NP minutes away."},"overflow":{"score":5,"why":"Endless cabins and hotels within 10 minutes."},"june":{"score":8,"why":"High 80s, humid, afternoon storms, heavy traffic; but cheap."}}',
