('estes-park','Estes Park / YMCA of the Rockies','Estes Park, CO','CO',40.377,-105.52,
 'The best fit on paper, held back by one thing: availability nine months out. The 8-bedroom retreat cabin at YMCA of the Rockies Estes Park Center sleeps up to 34 with 8.5 baths, on a campus that borders Rocky Mountain National Park with an indoor pool, climbing wall, mini golf, archery, horseback riding and a dining hall. Overflow is decisive: 583 lodge rooms and 230 family cabins 200 yards away. Comfortable, not luxurious, and Denver is the only airport on the list that is nonstop from all five origins.',
 '["Denver is nonstop from all five origins","Campus covers kid amenities, activities and overflow at once","Rocky Mountain NP at the door","Cool June weather"]',
 '["One flagship cabin; if it is gone there is no comparable backup","No theater, arcade or private hot tub: comfortable, not a mansion","Timed-entry reservations for the park; altitude sluggishness on day one","Trail Ridge Road can stay closed into June"]',
 '{"lodging":{"score":17,"why":"Single 8-BR retreat cabin; they recommend booking two years ahead for summer. Private-market fallback (Panorama, 6 BR) is thin."},"amenities":{"score":9,"why":"Indoor pool, roller rink, climbing wall, mini golf, playground on campus; nothing inside the cabin itself."},"travel":{"score":18,"why":"SEA-DEN nonstop ~2h45 + 1h45 drive, ~7 h. Denver nonstop from Nashville, Chicago, Milwaukee, Tampa and Fort Myers."},"kids":{"score":13,"why":"Campus activities for every age; park hikes; fewer rainy-day and theme-park options."},"nature":{"score":15,"why":"Adjacent to Rocky Mountain National Park."},"overflow":{"score":5,"why":"Hundreds of lodge rooms and cabins on the same campus."},"june":{"score":8,"why":"Dry and cool; some roads and trails still closed after a snowy winter."}}',
