('park-city-heber','Park City / Heber Valley','Park City, UT','UT',40.646,-111.50,
 'The direct answer to the Washington family''s objection: Salt Lake is nonstop from Seattle in about two hours and Park City is 40 minutes from the terminal, roughly 5.5 hours door to door. June is shoulder season in a ski town, so big homes rent at a fraction of winter rates and the weather is dry, 75 to 85 with cool nights. Utah Olympic Park, the alpine slide, Homestead Crater and Jordanelle reservoir cover the kids. What it lacks is national-park adjacency and lodging depth: 7-bedroom homes exist but are pricier and rarer than the Smokies.',
 '["Shortest travel day for Seattle by a wide margin","Dry, mild June; empty ski town","Olympic Park bobsled, zip line, alpine slide for the 11-year-old","Silver Springs Lodge (10 BR) is a strong single property"]',
 '["No national park within 3.5 hours","Thinner and pricier 7+ BR inventory; indoor pools rare","Fort Myers to SLC is seasonal"]',
